### 3.2. Enforce HTTPS & HSTS

If the app sits behind a reverse proxy (NGINX, Cloudflare, etc.):

```js
app.enable('trust proxy'); // required when behind a proxy
app.use((req, res, next) => {
  if (req.secure) {
    return next();
  }
  // Redirect HTTP → HTTPS
  res.redirect(`https://${req.headers.host}${req.originalUrl}`);
});
```

Then Helmet will automatically add `Strict-Transport-Security` headers.

*Result*: Addresses **A02 – Cryptographic Failures**.

---

### 3.3. Add Rate Limiting (Brute‑Force & DoS Protection)

```js
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');

const apiLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000, // 15 minutes
  max: 100,                 // limit each IP to 100 requests per window
  message: { error: 'Too many requests, please try again later.' },
  standardHeaders: true,
  legacyHeaders: false,
});

app.use('/users', apiLimiter); // apply only to sensitive endpoints
app.use(apiLimiter); // or globally, if you prefer
```

*Result*: Mitigates **A01 – Broken Access Control** (brute‑force) and **A05 – Security Misconfiguration** (rate‑limit DoS).

